          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-90691",
          ":question/problem": "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}}\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}(1+{v}^{3})}{{v}^{2}{x}^{3}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1+{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}}+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}} \\\\ {v}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {v}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{3} & =3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x|+3{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{3} & =3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we have let $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)}^{3} & =3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x|+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{{x}^{3}} & =3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x|+C \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{3}(3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x|+C) \\\\ y & =x\\sqrt[3]{3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x|+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
